            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">13. Remove Bullet Points</h2>

            <p>
                Set <code>list-style-type</code> to <code>none</code>
                when you want to remove the default bullets.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;ul style="list-style-type: none;"&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Home&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;About&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Contact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>
<h3 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">
    Output
</h3>

            <div class="example-box">
                <ul style="list-style-type: none; padding-left: 0;" class="mb-0">
                    <li>Home</li>
                    <li>About</li>
                    <li>Contact</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">14. Unordered List with CSS Class</h2>

            <p>
                It is usually better to use CSS classes instead of inline styles.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;style&gt;

    .course-list {
        list-style-type: square;
    }

&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;ul class="course-list"&gt;

    &lt;li&gt;HTML&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;CSS&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;JavaScript&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>


            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">15. Nested Unordered Lists</h2>

            <p>
                One unordered list can be placed inside another list item.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;ul&gt;

    &lt;li&gt;
        Frontend
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;HTML&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;CSS&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;JavaScript&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;

    &lt;li&gt;
        Backend
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;C#&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;.NET&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;SQL&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;

&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>
<h3 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">
    Output
</h3>

            <div class="example-box">
                <strong>Output:</strong>

                <ul class="mt-2 mb-0">
                    <li>
                        Frontend
                        <ul>
                            <li>HTML</li>
                            <li>CSS</li>
                            <li>JavaScript</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Backend
                        <ul>
                            <li>C#</li>
                            <li>.NET</li>
                            <li>SQL</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">16. Multi-Level Nested Lists</h2>

            <p>
                Lists can contain multiple levels of nested lists.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;ul&gt;

    &lt;li&gt;
        Web Development

        &lt;ul&gt;

            &lt;li&gt;
                Frontend

                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;HTML&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;CSS&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;JavaScript&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

            &lt;/li&gt;

            &lt;li&gt;
                Backend

                &lt;ul&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;C#&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;.NET&lt;/li&gt;
                    &lt;li&gt;SQL&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;/ul&gt;

            &lt;/li&gt;

        &lt;/ul&gt;

    &lt;/li&gt;

&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>


            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">17. Unordered List for Navigation</h2>

            <p>
                Navigation menus are often built using unordered lists.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;nav&gt;

    &lt;ul class="navigation"&gt;

        &lt;li&gt;
            &lt;a href="index.html"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;/li&gt;

        &lt;li&gt;
            &lt;a href="courses.html"&gt;Courses&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;/li&gt;

        &lt;li&gt;
            &lt;a href="about.html"&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;/li&gt;

        &lt;li&gt;
            &lt;a href="contact.html"&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;/li&gt;

    &lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;/nav&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>


            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">18. Horizontal Navigation with CSS</h2>

            <pre><code>&lt;style&gt;

    .navigation {
        list-style-type: none;
        padding: 0;
        margin: 0;
    }

    .navigation li {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-right: 20px;
    }

&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;nav&gt;

    &lt;ul class="navigation"&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#"&gt;Courses&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#"&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#"&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;/nav&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>


            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">19. Unordered List with Icons</h2>

            <p>
                CSS or icon libraries can be used to replace the default marker
                with a custom visual style.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;ul class="feature-list"&gt;

    &lt;li&gt;Fast Performance&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Responsive Design&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Easy Maintenance&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre>

            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold mt-4">Example CSS</h3>

            <pre><code>&lt;style&gt;

    .feature-list {
        list-style-type: none;
        padding: 0;
    }

    .feature-list li::before {
        content: "✓";
        margin-right: 8px;
    }

&lt;/style&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>


